# Machine-wide agent context

Use concise `AGENTS.md` files as the only active startup instructions. `CLAUDE.md` is deprecated: migrate unique current rules into the applicable `AGENTS.md`, then remove it.

## Project documentation

When creating, materially updating, or explicitly reviewing README or `AGENTS.md` files, read `~/git/agent-skills/docs/reference/project-documentation-standard.md` and apply it within the authorized scope. It is the shared convention, not an instruction to invoke a skill or rewrite other project documentation; preserve explicit project requirements and surface conflicts.

## Project roots and Pi sessions

Run Pi and project commands from the canonical project root. Pi stores and resumes sessions by exact working directory, so restart Pi from the correct root rather than changing directory only inside a shell command.

Use a stable component directory only when it is intentionally an independent project. Run cross-project work from its documented coordinator project, such as `agent-skills` for Project Portfolio, and keep target-project sessions separate.

## Shell and Windows/WSL boundaries

Use the destination OS's native shell: Bash inside Linux or WSL, and PowerShell for Windows-native automation. On the machine where Pi runs directly (including its local Windows/WSL boundary), require PowerShell 7 (`pwsh.exe`); never use Windows PowerShell 5.1 or Git Bash as a local fallback. This PowerShell 7 requirement does not apply to remote machines: use the remote machine's available PowerShell version, including Windows PowerShell 5.1, with compatible commands. Do not require a remote PowerShell upgrade solely to satisfy the local policy.

At Windows, MSYS, WSL, PowerShell, SSH, or unclear path boundaries, read `~/.pi/agent/lib/environment-support.md` and use the reviewed machine helpers it identifies. This is essential supporting machinery, not entry into an optional workflow. Ordinary same-shell commands need no environment probe. Use the managed launcher for consented long-running Windows-to-WSL Node jobs.

Name script runtimes in agent-facing commands: `node <script>`, `bash <script>`, `uv run`/`uvx`, or a native PowerShell `.ps1` entrypoint (PowerShell 7 locally; the available version remotely). Never invoke an extensionless script directly from PowerShell.

Pi 0.85+ built-in file tools resolve relative paths and supported Windows/WSL aliases against `ctx.cwd`; shell commands still use their shell's path namespace. Keep builds, installs, clones, and watchers on WSL ext4 under `~/git`, not `/mnt/c`.

{{ includeTemplate "agent-python-uv.md.tmpl" }}
The Pi `uv` extension enforces the mechanical boundary.

## Secrets (`ak`)

Approved low-risk secrets live in the GPG-encrypted vault for the WSL distro named by `~/.config/ak/vault.conf`. Never guess another distro, fall back to Windows Credential Manager, automate Bitwarden, print retrieved values, or store them in plaintext.

Prefer the consuming workflow's managed launcher. When manual retrieval is necessary, read `~/.pi/agent/lib/environment-support.md` and capture the approved helper inside the consuming command: Bash uses `bash ~/git/agent-skills/skills/windows-env/ak-get <SERVICE>`; PowerShell 7 uses `Get-AkSecret.ps1 -Service <SERVICE>`. Import only the reviewed `~/.envrc` allowlist.

## Windows tools and recovery

Jack keeps discoverable Windows tools and recovery kits under `C:\tools`. Keep project-specific layouts, recovery procedures, and implementation details in the owning repository's documentation, not machine-wide startup instructions.

## Windows clipboard and opening files

When the user says “snip”, “shot”, or “screenshot”, inspect the current Windows screenshot clipboard image through the machine helper {{ if eq .chezmoi.os "windows" }}`& ~/git/agent-skills/skills/windows-env/Invoke-WinClipboard.ps1 Snip`{{ else }}`bash ~/git/agent-skills/skills/windows-env/win-clipboard snip`{{ end }}. If no image is present, ask for a new `Win+Shift+S` snip. Use the path printed by the helper.

Use the machine helper {{ if eq .chezmoi.os "windows" }}`& ~/git/agent-skills/skills/windows-env/Invoke-WinOpen.ps1 <TARGET>`{{ else }}`bash ~/git/agent-skills/skills/windows-env/win-open <TARGET>`{{ end }} for Windows targets, not `xdg-open`. USB devices must be attached Windows-side with `usbipd` before WSL can access them.
